# Settings and API keys for luxd. Copy this file, fill in what you use,
# and keep the copy private:
#
#   install -m 600 .env.example ~/.config/lux/luxd.env
#
# `lux server start` loads ~/.config/lux/luxd.env automatically. To use a
# different file, pass it explicitly: lux server start --env-file .env
# (the real .env is git-ignored; never commit it). Variables already set in
# your shell win over the file. Empty values mean "not set".
#
# Keys stay inside luxd: agents get a short-lived run token instead.
# All settings: docs/self-hosting.md#configuration

# ---- Model providers (set the ones you use) ----

# Lyzr: an agent's model is lyzr:<lyzr-agent-id> in its agent.yaml.
LUX_LYZR_API_KEY=
# LUX_LYZR_BASE_URL=https://agent-prod.studio.lyzr.ai/v4

# Anthropic (Claude): model anthropic:<model>, e.g. anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-5
LUX_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# OpenAI: model openai:<model>
LUX_OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Ollama runs locally and needs no key.
# LUX_OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1
# LUX_OLLAMA_DISABLED=true

# Model keys can also be added in the app (… > Models); a key set here wins.

# ---- Connectors (people connect their own accounts under … > Connectors) ----
# Google, Microsoft 365 and Slack are usually set up by an administrator in
# the app (docs/connectors.md). Google can also be set here: an OAuth client
# ("Desktop app" for your own computer); people sign in through
#   <LUX_PUBLIC_URL>/v1/connectors/google/callback
# Tokens, app secrets and model keys entered in the app are encrypted with
# LUX_SECRET_KEY (openssl rand -base64 32); without it, luxd creates one in
# its data folder.
# LUX_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# LUX_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# LUX_SECRET_KEY=

# ---- Git (for repositories and private agents; see docs/git-workflows.md) ----
# Referred to by name, here "github": lux repo add NAME URL --credential github
# LUX_GIT_CREDENTIAL_GITHUB=

# ---- Database ----
# Usually saved once with: lux server start --database-url postgres://...
# LUX_DATABASE_URL=
